From 896bf86c57f35feb2c04588ac6a801b038362330 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Usty <usty@uase.tech>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:35:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] fix: tighten receipt/invoice/proforma template spacing
 so more documents fit naturally on fewer pages

Real gap addressed: font sizes in this template were already
appropriately small (7-22px range, mostly 8-13px for body text) - the
actual cumulative height problem was the whitespace BETWEEN
sections. Summed across a typical document (header, the two-column
info grid, vehicle details box, totals block, items table,
confirmation box, terms) the margins alone added up to roughly
100px+ of pure spacing.

Tightened every section's margin-bottom and internal padding
moderately (roughly 30% reduction throughout) without touching a
single font-size - reclaims meaningful vertical space while keeping
every line exactly as readable as before. Combined with the export
mechanism's own existing shrink-to-fit logic (documents up to 1.4x
one page's height get scaled to fit rather than split - deliberately
left that threshold unchanged, since pushing it further would risk
making the already-small 7-8px text illegible on genuinely longer
documents), this should mean more short receipts and invoices
naturally land on one page without needing to lean on that
image-shrink fallback as hard, and fewer borderline-length documents
tip over into needing a second page at all.
